B.RI=new A.H("Farmer Grandpa","Grandpa the farmer harvests rice. Help carry it to the barn.","Helping the old is a great kindness.",B.F)
B.Sr=new A.H("Rice Barn","Rice is stored for the hard season. Do not waste it.","Save and store for later \u2014 that is wise.",B.a1)
B.V0=new A.H("Grandma Tells Tales","Grandma tells village stories at night. Listen carefully.","Listen when elders speak \u2014 there is much wisdom there.",B.ab)
B.UM=new A.H("Morning Chores","The village chief feeds the cows before sunrise.","Wake early and work hard \u2014 the habit of great people.",B.F)
B.Sl=new A.H("Night Watch","The people guard the village at night, taking turns at the post.","Keeping your turn keeps everyone safe.",B.a1)
B.Sy=new A.H("New Friend","A child sits alone. Kiko invites them to play together.","Invite the lonely \u2014 no one likes being left out.",B.F)
B.SI=new A.H("Fair Chief","The village chief shares help fairly and openly with everyone.","A fair and honest leader is respected by all.",B.b0)
B.UZ=new A.H("The Midwife","The midwife helps a sick neighbor. She is amazing!","Those who help many people \u2014 respect and thank them.",B.ab)
B.Ux=new A.H("After the Rain","Heavy rain makes the road slippery and muddy. The people pitch in.","In hard times, helping each other speeds the recovery.",B.F)
B.TX=new A.H("Great Harvest","The whole village harvests together. The crop is shared fairly.","Work together, enjoy together \u2014 that is lovely.",B.a1)
B.RJ=new A.H("Village Hall","The village hall is cleaned for an event. Everyone helps sweep.","Public places are a shared duty \u2014 keep them clean.",B.V)
B.Th=new A.H("Harvest Feast","The village celebrates the harvest. All eat and laugh together.","Be thankful for the crop and share the joy with neighbors.",B.F)
B.Sf=new A.H("Farewell Greeting","Kiko says goodbye. Kiss the grandparents' hands before leaving.","Say a polite goodbye \u2014 a sign of love and respect.",B.ab)
B.Sh=new A.H("Village Friend","The last day in the mountains. The final boss awaits!","Respect for parents, teachers, and neighbors \u2014 that is who you are.",B.ab)
